## 0.17beta

### Enhancements
- Hardened the TCP/UDP transport: OS-level TCP keepalive to catch a silently
  dropped connection faster, exponential backoff on repeated UDP telemetry
  failures (was retrying every 1s forever), and UDP telemetry now verifies
  it's actually the amp sending the data before displaying it.
- Added rolling p50/p95 logging for command-confirm round-trip time and
  telemetry frame cadence, to support future tuning decisions with real
  numbers instead of guesses.

### Changed
- Removed the bundled Npcap driver installer. Cold connects lose the
  broadcast-ARP latency fix it enabled (falls back to the slower default
  ARP path, ~15-18s worst case) but the installer no longer silently
  installs a third-party network driver.

## 0.16beta

### Enhancements
- Compact view redesigned: Reflected/Drive/Current moved into the Forward
  Power card as compact mini-gauges, antenna buttons relocated into the
  same row, and the window now locks to an exact-fit size instead of
  leaving dead space from a stale saved geometry.
- Topbar now follows the selected theme (light/dark/colorblind/high-
  contrast) instead of always rendering as a fixed dark bar.
- First-run Setup dialog's serial connection field replaced with a
  detected-COM-ports dropdown (plus rescan), instead of typing a port
  name blind.
- Added Report a Bug / Request a Feature buttons under Setup > Diagnostics,
  pre-filled with app version and connection type.
- Trimmed scapy's import cost in the startup ARP-priming path (~180ms
  faster app launch, measured).

### Bug Fixes
- Fixed Compact-view text clipping/squeezing at text-scale settings above
  the default (antenna/band label and meter value boxes).
- Fixed inconsistent lowercase "w" units on Reflected/Drive tiles.
- Fixed a CSS comment accidentally closed early by its own content, which
  had been silently dropping the entire light-theme variable block.
- Fixed three hover states that were invisible against the new light-theme
  topbar.
- Fixed compiler.iss having a hardcoded developer-machine path, which made
  the installer fail to build on any other machine.

## 0.15beta

### Enhancements
- Reduced redundant JSON encoding in the WebSocket broadcast path (status/
  telemetry events were being encoded twice per event, then re-encoded
  again per connected client) - fewer encode passes on the hot path that
  fires on every status reply and multiple times per second during TX.

### Bug Fixes
- Fixed a live telemetry timestamp mismatch: the value shown live and the
  value later replayed from history could disagree because each encoding
  pass independently sampled the clock.
- Hardened WINUSB cleanup on a failed connect (removed a redundant/riskier
  interface-release call that could mask the real error) and fixed a
  Windows build incorrectly checking for a Linux-only timeout error code.
